cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "csd-lean4: a Lean 4 formalisation of Constraint-Surface Dynamics"
abstract: >-
  Machine-verified reconstruction of finite-dimensional quantum mechanics from a
  deterministic ontic surface carrying a Liouville measure and a
  measure-preserving flow, with the Born rule derived as a volume ratio.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Blore
    given-names: Zayn
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-8447-7247"
    email: zayn.blore@ou.ac.uk
repository-code: "https://github.com/zblore/csd-lean4"
url: "https://constraintsurfacedynamics.com"
license: Apache-2.0
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.22232291"
    description: >-
      Concept DOI. Always resolves to the latest release. This is the one to
      cite. Zenodo also mints a per-version DOI on every release
      (10.5281/zenodo.22232292 for v1.5.0); do not cite those -- a reader who
      follows a version DOI lands on a snapshot and cannot see that the
      corpus moved. No `version:` or `date-released:` key is set here on
      purpose: the concept DOI already tracks the latest release, and a
      hand-maintained version string in this file is precisely the kind of
      claim that has gone stale three times (see the guarded line below).
keywords:
  - lean4
  - mathlib
  - formal-verification
  - quantum-foundations
  - born-rule
  - quantum-mechanics
  - interactive-theorem-proving
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Citing a THEOREM rather than the software as a whole.
#
# Formal results in this repository are cited by naming, together:
#
#   1. this repository (the `repository-code` URL below),
#   2. a tag, or failing that the exact commit SHA,
#   3. the module path, e.g. `CsdLean4/LF6/C1BellConsistency.lean`,
#   4. the fully-qualified theorem name, e.g.
#      `CSD.LF6.no_compatible_global_chsh_assignment_realises_singlet`.
#
# That quadruple is reproducible: the toolchain and Mathlib revision are pinned
# in `lean-toolchain` and `lakefile.toml` at that commit, so the theorem can be
# rechecked exactly as stated.
#
# DO NOT cite the manuscript layers "LF5" or "LF6" as documents. They are
# unpublished, and citing them would be a dependency-order violation. The
# repository is one artefact with its own DOI -- 10.5281/zenodo.22232291,
# the concept DOI recorded under `identifiers` above -- and citing it at a tag
# is not.
# See `docs/C1-FORMAL-SUPPORT.md` for the claim-to-theorem map.
#
# C1 formal support: cite tag `v1.4.1-c1-complete`, together with the
# exact module path and fully-qualified theorem name. The revised paper's pair:
# CL-031 `CSD.LF6.no_compatible_global_chsh_assignment_realises_singlet` (the
# general obstruction) + CL-052 `CSD.LF6.c1_singlet_contextual_capstone` (the
# positive half: existence and obstruction in one statement), both in
# `CsdLean4/LF6/C1BellConsistency.lean`.
#
# ⚠️ THIS LINE HAS GONE STALE THREE TIMES (at R2, at R3, and through the whole
# v1.4.x pair — found 2026-08-17). Its "update it in the same commit" instruction
# demonstrably does not self-execute, so it is now GUARDED: `check-claims.sh`
# check (13) fails when the newest `v*-c1-*` tag is not the one this line names.
#
# "tag", not "tagged release": the C1 anchors are git TAGS and none of them is a
# published GitHub Release. Exactly one release exists (v1.5.0-c2-support, the one
# Zenodo archived), so "tagged release" was ambiguous in a repo where the Releases
# page lists one entry and the Tags page lists two dozen. A tag is what the citation
# quadruple actually needs -- immutable and resolvable -- and it is what to cite.
# Policy set 2026-09-01: tags are published as Releases going forward where that is
# warranted; older tags are deliberately NOT retro-released, because Zenodo orders a
# concept record by publication order and back-filling would repoint the concept DOI
# at an old snapshot.
# Cutting a C1 tag therefore requires updating this line in the same stroke, on
# pain of CI.
#
# Tag history — do NOT move or delete these; they are audit history, and each is
# immutable by design:
#   v1.2.0-c1-correction  the C1 correction itself (superseded prose)
#   v1.2.1-c1-R1          first hygiene pass (still has the old endpoint text)
#   v1.2.2-c1-R2          endpoint treatment corrected
#   v1.2.3-c1-R3          live-documentation residuals closed, wingPairUnitary
#                         unitarity exported, prose-audit guard mode 4 added
#                         (superseded: its "final C1 repository tag" note
#                         predated the two-sided separation)
#   v1.3.0-consolidation  Q1-Q5/Q7/Q15 consolidation release (not C1-specific)
#   v1.4.0-c1-two-sided   CL-052 lands: the explicit contextual model; superseded
#                         same-week by v1.4.1 (predates Q20 and the notation
#                         bridge)
#   v1.4.1-c1-complete    CURRENT — the complete C1 stack: CL-031 + CL-052, the
#                         Q20 section-4/5.1 theorems, the SigmaSpace/Bell-Lambda
#                         notation bridge
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

